                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "123558e6-3002-4780-ab53-7c76f11bf62a",
                        "entry_id": "f2b7fb75-9c6d-394a-9601-506e5c90905b",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Mentoresse"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6af5ec39-2b81-3eed-a998-f377cf16ec9d",
                        "entry_id": "f2b7fb75-9c6d-394a-9601-506e5c90905b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celle qui sert de guide ou de conseillère à quelqu’un."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47c60e89-3b67-474a-b0d7-1010f29ea4a3",
                                "sense_id": "6af5ec39-2b81-3eed-a998-f377cf16ec9d",
                                "text": "— T’as pas l’impression qu’on exagère ? dis-je à ma « mentoresse »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "419bf3b6-c96e-40a0-a4d4-11755daf362b",
                        "source_entry_id": "f2b7fb75-9c6d-394a-9601-506e5c90905b",
                        "source_sense_id": "6af5ec39-2b81-3eed-a998-f377cf16ec9d",
                        "target_lang_word": "mentoress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mentoress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52cd98ab-dc5c-3031-b279-3e7266611d27",
                                        "entry_id": "abaced55-cb14-3fc8-b0c8-024d65ef6bf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female mentor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee93fb79-1021-4d1b-a348-9d3650e7925f",
                                                "sense_id": "52cd98ab-dc5c-3031-b279-3e7266611d27",
                                                "text": "“Whatever temptation Plutus may offer,” said my worldly mentoress, “never, Lionel, let the golden bait induce you to marry any girl whose antecedents you must have to explain—whom you must be the first to introduce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3b45f9a-78cc-468d-88e9-14d021fa63aa",
                                                "sense_id": "52cd98ab-dc5c-3031-b279-3e7266611d27",
                                                "text": "“Men admire you in the ball-room,” say the mentors and mentoresses, “but they choose a wife from the home-circle.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbf4f088-6252-448d-bac8-9871a7c2235c",
                                                "sense_id": "52cd98ab-dc5c-3031-b279-3e7266611d27",
                                                "text": "2. Employ outside freelance consultants for relatively higher fees rather than using an in-house employee, because: / • Good mentoresses are hard to find. / • A mentoress should be experienced in a variety of issues. / • Emotional knowledge is constantly changing. / • You may use different mentoresses for different assignments."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80cfe9ba-aa73-4793-9e91-925d141b4f1c",
                        "source_entry_id": "f2b7fb75-9c6d-394a-9601-506e5c90905b",
                        "source_sense_id": "6af5ec39-2b81-3eed-a998-f377cf16ec9d",
                        "target_lang_word": "mentress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mentress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6920aa76-1d9a-300a-a246-b9a048ee38d3",
                                        "entry_id": "c50092f1-c54d-3161-b143-efcaa4b1fd9e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of mentoress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03acd36c-2caa-4663-a8e4-e6298ca49b6e",
                                                "sense_id": "6920aa76-1d9a-300a-a246-b9a048ee38d3",
                                                "text": "“Jane Addams had lived in that higher dreamland of the future, ahead of her country women, ahead even of those who assumed to be the mentress of her people, as does every noble soul that labors “to make the bounds of freedom wider yet.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afb38822-c0ff-4439-b495-d24e8711d4be",
                                                "sense_id": "6920aa76-1d9a-300a-a246-b9a048ee38d3",
                                                "text": "[…]makes some comments about his mentress \"Satura\" which imply critical distinctions.[…]His Varronian satire is a philosophical dialogue, in the Socratic tradition of instruction; his mentress is \"Satyra.\"[…]Philosophy, for instance, instead of being the mentress of the satirist, became a shadow cast only in the light of an understanding of the distortion of tradition that took place in the writings of the critics."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e5cfaf3-0ac8-42fc-a9c2-8d9022b179c8",
                                                "sense_id": "6920aa76-1d9a-300a-a246-b9a048ee38d3",
                                                "text": "“Grow up: I have this theory, hey, about why women don’t need mentors.” / “Mentresses …” / “Men-tors. Mentor was a person’s name. Can’t say … I don’t know …[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04964f6f-1830-4fb0-afba-25229ba9a837",
                                                "sense_id": "6920aa76-1d9a-300a-a246-b9a048ee38d3",
                                                "text": "“Did you have any female mentors?” she asks. / “Female what?” / “Like, teachers, or other woman painters you admired.” / “Shouldn’t that be mentresses?” I say nastily. “There weren’t any. My teacher was a man.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eafb9255-71bf-4e7a-b222-36a1869f204f",
                                                "sense_id": "6920aa76-1d9a-300a-a246-b9a048ee38d3",
                                                "text": "I also hope very much that they will find en route their own mentors and mentresses in their quest for peace, justice and equality between men and women around the globe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "22861d26-85cf-4572-8b56-dd2110e6df55",
                        "source_entry_id": "f2b7fb75-9c6d-394a-9601-506e5c90905b",
                        "source_sense_id": "6af5ec39-2b81-3eed-a998-f377cf16ec9d",
                        "target_lang_word": "mentrix",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mentrix",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a25a442d-caff-3fce-b01e-386c29a176cd",
                                        "entry_id": "da19de44-e70f-343d-af00-e8150f6c853a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female mentor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48013dc4-16a9-462a-b81b-4ce9f8977f95",
                                                "sense_id": "a25a442d-caff-3fce-b01e-386c29a176cd",
                                                "text": "Olga had indeed learned that the church had appointed certain days and seasons for fasting, but thought she had herself fasted in a fashion, she had never suspected that she was imitating Christ, and she had never been told that the oil was a necessary part of the observance. Anxious to please her new mentrix she tried to swallow the nasty stuff, but the flesh was weak and, moreover, rebellious; and thus the first experiment in religious discipline proved a failure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1febbb99-3843-4a13-ae51-57f74d70c461",
                                                "sense_id": "a25a442d-caff-3fce-b01e-386c29a176cd",
                                                "text": "Finally, as women scholars — at every career level — we must never underestimate our value as mentors — or mentrices."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb8876f2-bfce-4a05-9298-9b8f47142b95",
                                                "sense_id": "a25a442d-caff-3fce-b01e-386c29a176cd",
                                                "text": "But shouldn't the verb form be \"ment\"? The mentor mented his mentees. / His wife, also a mentrix, or one of his daughters, both mentrices, took over menting when he was away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81c954c4-37aa-416b-aba1-10cf98f5918d",
                                                "sense_id": "a25a442d-caff-3fce-b01e-386c29a176cd",
                                                "text": "Each girl is instructed by a mentrix (nacimbusa, plural banacimbusa), who is helped by other women. Apart from being themselves initiated and authorized to perform these rites, the mentrices must be women who are well-respected in society, who maintain a good standard of family life, and whose conduct is above reproach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94f9862f-f918-4637-ae34-45be077ac559",
                                                "sense_id": "a25a442d-caff-3fce-b01e-386c29a176cd",
                                                "text": "One of my mentors (mentrixes? mentrices?), fantasy-horror novelist Chelsea Quinn Yarbro, who proudly claims Finnish heritage*, asserts quite strongly that the Finns are not Scandinavians. They certainly aren't Slavs either."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
